    {
      "title": "Musk says he was behind Starlink speed curbs after Ukraine service restored",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/musk-says-he-was-behind-starlink-speed-curbs-after-ukraine-service-restored-126102500019_1.html",
      "description": "Ukraine's access to Starlink and Starshield satellite links has been restored to the speeds it had before restrictions that disrupted front-line operations for more than a week, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said on Saturday.\n\"The speeds are now where they need to be,\" Zelenskyy wrote on X, adding that restoration began overnight and were sufficient by Saturday morning, improving front-line logistics and defence against Russian jet-powered Shahed drones.\nMusk admits he was behind Starlink's speed restriction\nAfter Ukraine said the services had been restored, Elon Musk spoke out on the speed restrictions that began last week. In a post on Saturday on X, Musk acknowledged that his company, SpaceX, throttled the Starlink satellite internet service.\n\"Using Starlink, a civilian commercial service, for offensive drone strikes to kill people has never been allowed, nor should it be,\" Musk wrote. \"Ukraine military violated Starlink terms of service and used it for offensive drone",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
